  "Question": "The angles of quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\) satisfy \\(\\angle A = 2\\angle B = 3\\angle C = 4\\angle D.\\) What is the degree measure of \\(\\angle A,\\) rounded to the nearest whole number?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(125\\)",
    "B": "\\(144\\)",
    "C": "\\(153\\)",
    "D": "\\(173\\)",
    "E": "\\(180\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The given equalities express all four angles in terms of \\(\\angle A\\):\n\\[\n\\angle B=\\frac{\\angle A}{2},\\qquad\n\\angle C=\\frac{\\angle A}{3},\\qquad\n\\angle D=\\frac{\\angle A}{4}.\n\\]\nThus their ratio is\n\\[\n1:\\frac12:\\frac13:\\frac14\n=12:6:4:3.\n\\]\nA quadrilateral’s interior angles sum to \\(360^\\circ\\). The ratio contains \\(12+6+4+3=25\\) equal parts, of which \\(\\angle A\\) receives \\(12\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\angle A=\\frac{12}{25}\\cdot360^\\circ\n=172.8^\\circ.\n\\]\nSince the tenths digit is \\(8\\), rounding to the nearest whole degree gives \\(\\boxed{173^\\circ}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
